SUMMARY:Hydra Carnival parade to Kamini
LOCATION:Hydra Town / Kamini\, Hydra\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the last Sunday of Apokries the islanders parade in fancy dress from the harbour along the coast path to Kamini\, with music\, a giant papier-mâché head and horsemen (and donkeys\, this being Hydra)\, ending at the tavernas of Kamini. Tsiknopempti before it means street barbecues on the port. Ferries from Piraeus run all winter\, and rooms are at their cheapest.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/hydra/#hydra-town-kamini-hydra-carnival-parade-to-kamini
